  "report_period": "Week 21 (16th May to 23rd May 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Oldendorff Carriers have committed their Newcastlemax \"Luise Oldendorff\" 207/2015 Hyundai, Korea (SS 05/2030, DD 04/2028, Scrubber fitted) to clients of HMM at USD 51 mill. For reference, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Linda Oldendorff\" 207/2014 Hyundai, Korea (SS 09/2029, DD 08/2027, Scrubber fitted) was sold back in December at USD 48,3 mill. The Capesize \"Thalassini Agatha\" 182/2011 Universal, Japan (SS 01/2026, DD 11/2025, Scrubber fitted) of Enesel was committed at USD 28,8 mill. For comparison, the one-year-older \"Mount Austin\" 178/2010 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 06/2025, Scrubber fitted) was sold back in March at USD 27,5 mill. Moreover, Seanergy Maritime committed their \"Tradership\" 176/2006 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 07/2025) to Chinese interests at USD 18,5 mill. Note that in April, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Arabella\" 177/2005 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 02/2028, DD 02/2026, Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 18 mill. On the Supramax sector, Susesea Holdings committed their \"Soldoy\" 56/2011 Yangfan, China (SS/DD 07/2026) at USD 12,5 mill, while the \"SFL Sara\" 56/2011 Xiamen, China (SS/DD 02/2026) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 11,5 mill. Moreover, Pacific Basin Shipping committed their \"Swan River\" 56/2005 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 07/2025, Scrubber fitted) at USD 10 mill. Remind you that back in March, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Strange Attractor\" 55/2006 Mitsui, Japan (SS 10/2026, DD 07/2025, Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 9,5 mill. The Handysize \"Siena\" 32/2002 Kanda, Japan (SS/DD 07/2025) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 5,8 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Achilles Bulker\" 32/2003 Kanda, Japan (SS 10/2028, DD 03/2027) was sold at USD 6,6 mill.",
    "tankers": "Angelicoussis have committed their VLCC \"Maran Canopus\" 320/2007 Daewoo, Korea (SS 09/2027, DD 01/2026, Scrubber fitted) at USD 49 mill. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the \"Layla\" 317/2007 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 08/2027, DD 09/2025) was sold at USD 46,75 mill. The MR2 \"STI Regina\" 50/2014 Spp, Korea (SS 09/2029, DD 09/2027, Scrubber fitted) of Scorpio Tankers was committed to clients of GESCO at USD 31 mill. Remind you that the one-year-younger \"Nord Swift\" 49/2015 Stx, Korea (SS/DD 09/2025, Scrubber fitted) was sold in March at USD 33,25 mill. In addition, NYK Line's \"World Navigator\" 46/2010 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 07/2025) was committed at region USD 17 mill, while the sister vessel \"Tamiat Navigator\" 46/2010 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 08/2025) was sold a month ago at region USD 18 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of high usd 7,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 10,000/12,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 10,000/13,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. South East Asian trips via South America into China were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Indian coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into China were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 18,000/20,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/700K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A generally quiet week for this segment. Trips from China into US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 11,000/13,000 pd range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from China into Australia were reported at the level of usd 9,000/11,000 pd. South East Asian trips into China were fixed around usd 8,000/11,000 pd. Continental trips into South America were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into Continent were fixed around usd 6,000/8,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 12,000/15,000 pd. South American coastal trips were fixed around usd 13,000/16,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
